runce — the drill for the fold fix, 2026-09-07
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

WHAT THIS WAS FOR. runcd (2026-09-07) found a fold that produced a pack
missing thirteen commits its inputs held, stopped naming those inputs,
and left forge refusing to serve. The fix is aaffe335: a fold's commit
may unname an input only if the roll-up HOLDS everything that input
holds. P5 — cold start — is the leg that exposed the defect, and it is
the oracle here.

SHAPE. trove project 144 `runce`, CP + 2 workers, ALL SPOT i4i.xlarge,
us-west-1. FORGE ONLY; walgit was not deployed (its arm costs a 949 MB
on-cluster build and compares nothing these legs need).
Image drill-aaffe335, verified BY DIGEST on the running pods:
