# Pre-registration — runce, the drill for the fold fix
Written 2026-09-06 23:2x UTC, BEFORE the cluster served a single push.
Cluster: trove project 144 `runce`, CP + 2 workers, ALL SPOT i4i.xlarge, us-west-1.
Image: drill-aaffe335 (HEAD). Arms: FORGE ONLY — walgit is not deployed.

## Why forge only
P5, P11 and P10 are forge-specific behaviours; walgit has no comparable undo
and its cold start was already measured. walgit's arm costs a 949 MB image
built on-cluster, which put a node under DiskPressure on runcd. The one leg
that genuinely wants a control arm is the ref ladder, and its honest control
is the local rig (see prereg-packrefs.md), not walgit.
CONSEQUENCE, STATED UP FRONT: P12 here has no in-run control, so any
comparison to runcd's ladder is CROSS-RUN and therefore suggestive at best.

## The leg that matters
P5 is the oracle. On runcd, deleting forge's pod made the successor REFUSE to
serve (exit 78, crash-loop, 10 restarts) because a fold had superseded the
only packs holding thirteen commits. The fix is the strict supersede rule.

Order: P0, P9, P2, P12, P5, P11, P10. P9 and P2 come FIRST ON PURPOSE — they
are the load that drives compaction. A P5 run against a repository that never
folded proves nothing, and that vacuity is the trap this rig has fallen into
before.

## Predictions
1. **P5 PASSES.** The successor restores, proves the repository and serves;
   no exit 78, no crash-loop. FALSIFIER: any refusal or restart loop. This is
   the prediction the whole fix stands on.
2. **`foldsRefused` may be NON-ZERO and that is NOT a failure.** It counts
   roll-ups the coverage check rejected BEFORE upload. Non-zero means the
   check is doing work; zero means git never lost an object on this workload.
   I pre-register that I will not read non-zero as a defect.
3. **P2's resident bytes will be EQUAL OR HIGHER than runcd's 1.44 GB**, not
   lower. The strict rule keeps more packs named, so less is collected. This
   is the known cost of the fix and I want it measured, not hidden. A large
   regression here is a real finding against the fix.
4. **P11 undo:** a force-push's previous tip is recoverable from the bucket
   and `--undo-list` names it.
5. **P10 outage:** with the bucket cut off, NO PUSH IS ACKED THAT IS NOT
   DURABLE — Inv_AckedIsDurable on the wire. Reads may continue from local
   packs; readiness may fail; recovery restores service. An ack of a push
   that is not in the bucket is a FAILURE of the central claim.
6. **P12:** forge's ladder at or below runcd's 0.28 / 0.43 / 0.74 s at
   0 / 2005 / 8010 refs. Cross-run, so a same-or-slower result does not by
   itself refute the pack-refs change.

